      "problem": "Rewrite the expression $({y}^{2}-24y+144)+5$ as the sum of a perfect square and a constant.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following formula:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2ay+{a}^{2}=(y-a)^{2}\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a perfect square in the parentheses that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-24y+144 & = \\\\ {y}^{2}-24y+{12}^{2} & = \\\\ {y}^{2}-2\\cdot 12y+{12}^{2} & = \\\\ (y-12)^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}^{2}-24y+144)+5 & = \\\\ (y-12)^{2}+5 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
